# flickos-layouts 1.53: check tests a see-through panel color; sfwbar: the
# dock (a Depends of flickos-layouts too); gnome-themes-extra-data: the
# Adwaita folder with gtk-3.0 that flickos-layout looks for (the theme itself
# is built into GTK 3); elementary-icon-theme and fonts-inter-variable: the
# icons Elemental names and the font of its bar and dock (1.7 MB, not the
# 21 MB fonts-inter).
Depends: flickos-layouts (>= 1.53),
         sfwbar,
         gnome-themes-extra-data,
         elementary-icon-theme,
         fonts-inter-variable,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Elemental style for the FlickOS desktop
 A light style for FlickOS: windows in one light grey (GTK's Adwaita)
 with the elementary icons, the title in the middle and plain buttons, a
 see-through dark top bar with white text, a dark slate terminal, a light
 app launcher and notifications, and a seashore seen from above with
 FlickOS's halo.
 .
 Its layout has a thin top bar with Applications on the left and the date
 and time in the middle, a light dock at the bottom, and the close button
 on the left of the title bar and maximize on the right.
 .
 Installing it adds Elemental to Desktop Layout & Style; Software's Use sets
 the style and the layout together.
